Contents:
* block-full-trackingON-dist_op_TORC_plasmid_st3.3_02_df.pkl
  Contains organized raw data resulted from TORCPhysics.
  This pickle file is dictionary, with each entry corresponding to the simulations of a particular system,
  e.g., EColi WT, Salmonella dtopA, etc...

* get_supercoiling_at_promoter.py
  This script loads the pickle file and extracts the superhelical values at the promoter when is active.
  That is when RNAPs bind and form either the closed or open complex.
  It also plots these distributions per promoter/gene
  This scripts outputs superhelicity_at_promoter.pkl

 * superhelicity_at_promoter.pkl
   It is a dictionary, with each entry corresponding to the superhelical values at each promoter.